Implement user story SKY-004-b: Create styled dashboard HTML and configure build/start scripts with static asset copying

## Story Description
Create src/public/index.html as a real styled single-page dashboard matching the specified layout, implement the GET / route in server.ts that reads and serves this file via fs.readFileSync at runtime (not hardcoded), and configure package.json with 'start' and 'build' scripts where the build copies src/public/ → dist/public/ so the dashboard is served correctly in both dev (tsx) and production (node dist/server.js) modes.

## Acceptance Criteria
- GET / → 200 text/html with body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read via fs.readFileSync at runtime (not a hardcoded/duplicated inline HTML string); never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- src/public/index.html is a styled dashboard with: (1) full-width blue (#1a73e8) header bar with bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and subtitle; (2) centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, padding) with 2-col grid form — From/To IATA inputs row 1, Date/Adults inputs row 2, each with label; (3) full-width search button same color as header; (4) status area with pink error banner, gray empty message, success count; (5) client-side JS fetching /search without page reload and rendering results
- package.json has 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js' and 'build' script that produces dist/server.js so `npm run build && npm run start` starts the server and GET /health returns 200
- Build script copies src/public/ → dist/public/; after `npm run build`, dist/public/index.html exists and GET / serves the real dashboard file (not 404 or stale fallback)
- supertest and @types/supertest listed in package.json devDependencies





